{"k":"trig","t":"Trigonometric Ratios & Identities","cls":"11","u":"Trigonometry","s":[["Basics and graphs",[{"q":"Radian–degree conversion","f":"\\pi\\ \\text{rad}=180^\\circ,\\qquad l=r\\theta","n":"Area of a sector $=\\frac12r^2\\theta$."},{"q":"Pythagorean identities","f":"\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta=1,\\quad 1+\\tan^2\\theta=\\sec^2\\theta,\\quad1+\\cot^2\\theta=\\csc^2\\theta","n":"$\\sec\\theta+\\tan\\theta=\\frac1{\\sec\\theta-\\tan\\theta}$ (useful pair trick)."},{"q":"Signs in quadrants","f":"\\text{I: all}+,\\ \\ \\text{II: }\\sin,\\csc+,\\ \\ \\text{III: }\\tan,\\cot+,\\ \\ \\text{IV: }\\cos,\\sec+","h":"\"All Students Take Coffee\"."},{"q":"Graph of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$","f":"\\sin x,\\cos x\\in[-1,1],\\ \\text{period }2\\pi","g":"y=sin(x) | y=cos(x) ; -6.6,6.6,-1.6,1.6"},{"q":"Graph of $\\tan x$","f":"\\tan x\\in\\mathbb R,\\ \\text{period }\\pi,\\ \\text{asymptotes } x=(2n+1)\\tfrac\\pi2","g":"y=tan(x) ; -4.8,4.8,-4,4"},{"q":"Graphs of $\\csc x$, $\\sec x$, $\\cot x$","f":"\\csc x,\\sec x\\in(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty),\\quad\\cot x\\in\\mathbb R","g":"y=1/sin(x) | y=1/cos(x) | y=1/tan(x) ; -6.6,6.6,-4,4"},{"q":"Allied angles (reduction)","f":"\\sin(\\pi-\\theta)=\\sin\\theta,\\ \\cos(\\pi-\\theta)=-\\cos\\theta,\\ \\sin(\\tfrac\\pi2-\\theta)=\\cos\\theta,\\ \\sin(-\\theta)=-\\sin\\theta","n":"Odd multiple of $\\frac\\pi2$: the function changes to its co-function; even multiple: it stays. Sign from the quadrant of the original angle."},{"q":"Standard values","f":"\\sin15^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt3-1}{2\\sqrt2},\\quad\\cos15^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt3+1}{2\\sqrt2},\\quad\\tan15^\\circ=2-\\sqrt3,\\quad\\tan75^\\circ=2+\\sqrt3"},{"q":"Values for 18°, 36°","f":"\\sin18^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt5-1}4,\\qquad\\cos36^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt5+1}4","n":"$\\cos18^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt{10+2\\sqrt5}}4$, $\\sin36^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt{10-2\\sqrt5}}4$.","d":"Let $\\theta=18^\\circ$: $2\\theta=90^\\circ-3\\theta \\Rightarrow \\sin2\\theta=\\cos3\\theta \\Rightarrow 2\\sin\\theta=4\\cos^2\\theta-3$ → $4\\sin^2\\theta+2\\sin\\theta-1=0$."},{"q":"Values for 22.5°, 7.5°","f":"\\tan22.5^\\circ=\\sqrt2-1,\\qquad\\tan67.5^\\circ=\\sqrt2+1","n":"$\\sin22.5^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt2}}2$, $\\cos22.5^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt2}}2$."},{"q":"Standard angle table","f":"\\begin{array}{c|ccccc}\\theta&0&\\frac\\pi6&\\frac\\pi4&\\frac\\pi3&\\frac\\pi2\\\\\\hline\\sin&0&\\frac12&\\frac1{\\sqrt2}&\\frac{\\sqrt3}2&1\\\\\\cos&1&\\frac{\\sqrt3}2&\\frac1{\\sqrt2}&\\frac12&0\\\\\\tan&0&\\frac1{\\sqrt3}&1&\\sqrt3&\\infty\\end{array}"},{"q":"Ranges of the six functions","f":"\\sin,\\cos\\in[-1,1];\\quad\\tan,\\cot\\in\\mathbb R;\\quad\\sec,\\csc\\in(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty)"},{"q":"Domains of the six functions","f":"\\tan,\\sec:\\ x\\ne(2n+1)\\tfrac\\pi2;\\qquad\\cot,\\csc:\\ x\\ne n\\pi"},{"q":"Even/odd nature","f":"\\cos,\\sec\\ \\text{even};\\quad\\sin,\\tan,\\cot,\\csc\\ \\text{odd}"},{"q":"Values for $54°$, $72°$","f":"\\sin54^\\circ=\\cos36^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt5+1}4,\\qquad\\cos72^\\circ=\\sin18^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt5-1}4"},{"q":"Values for $7.5°$","f":"\\tan7\\tfrac12^\\circ=\\sqrt6-\\sqrt3+\\sqrt2-2,\\qquad\\cot7\\tfrac12^\\circ=\\sqrt6+\\sqrt3+\\sqrt2+2"},{"q":"Graph of $\\sin x$ in degrees / periodicity table","f":"\\sin(x+2\\pi)=\\sin x,\\ \\tan(x+\\pi)=\\tan x;\\quad|\\sin x|\\ \\text{period}\\ \\pi","g":"y=abs(sin(x)) | y=abs(cos(x)) ; -6.5,6.5,-0.3,1.4"}]],["Compound angles",[{"q":"Sine of sum/difference","f":"\\sin(A\\pm B)=\\sin A\\cos B\\pm\\cos A\\sin B"},{"q":"Cosine of sum/difference","f":"\\cos(A\\pm B)=\\cos A\\cos B\\mp\\sin A\\sin B"},{"q":"Tangent of sum/difference","f":"\\tan(A\\pm B)=\\frac{\\tan A\\pm\\tan B}{1\\mp\\tan A\\tan B}","n":"$\\cot(A\\pm B)=\\frac{\\cot A\\cot B\\mp1}{\\cot B\\pm\\cot A}$."},{"q":"Product identities","f":"\\sin(A+B)\\sin(A-B)=\\sin^2A-\\sin^2B,\\qquad\\cos(A+B)\\cos(A-B)=\\cos^2A-\\sin^2B"},{"q":"Tangent of three angles","f":"\\tan(A+B+C)=\\frac{\\sum\\tan A-\\prod\\tan A}{1-\\sum\\tan A\\tan B}"},{"q":"$\\sin(A+B+C)$ and $\\cos(A+B+C)$","f":"\\sin(A+B+C)=\\sum\\sin A\\cos B\\cos C-\\sin A\\sin B\\sin C","n":"$\\cos(A+B+C)=\\cos A\\cos B\\cos C-\\sum\\cos A\\sin B\\sin C$."},{"q":"$\\tan(A+B)$ shortcuts with $45°$","f":"\\tan\\left(\\frac\\pi4+A\\right)=\\frac{1+\\tan A}{1-\\tan A}=\\frac{\\cos A+\\sin A}{\\cos A-\\sin A}","n":"If $A+B=\\frac\\pi4$: $(1+\\tan A)(1+\\tan B)=2$. If $A+B=\\frac{3\\pi}4$: $(1-\\tan A)(1-\\tan B)=2$."},{"q":"$\\cos^2A-\\sin^2B$ and $\\sin^2A-\\sin^2B$","f":"\\sin^2A-\\sin^2B=\\sin(A+B)\\sin(A-B),\\qquad\\cos^2A-\\sin^2B=\\cos(A+B)\\cos(A-B)"},{"q":"$\\tan A-\\tan B$ and $\\tan A+\\tan B$","f":"\\tan A\\pm\\tan B=\\frac{\\sin(A\\pm B)}{\\cos A\\cos B}"},{"q":"$\\cot A-\\tan A$ and $\\cot A+\\tan A$","f":"\\cot A-\\tan A=2\\cot2A,\\qquad\\cot A+\\tan A=2\\csc2A"}]],["Multiple and sub-multiple angles",[{"q":"Double angle","f":"\\sin2A=2\\sin A\\cos A=\\frac{2\\tan A}{1+\\tan^2A},\\quad\\cos2A=\\cos^2A-\\sin^2A=\\frac{1-\\tan^2A}{1+\\tan^2A}","n":"$\\cos2A=2\\cos^2A-1=1-2\\sin^2A$; $\\tan2A=\\frac{2\\tan A}{1-\\tan^2A}$."},{"q":"Triple angle","f":"\\sin3A=3\\sin A-4\\sin^3A,\\quad\\cos3A=4\\cos^3A-3\\cos A,\\quad\\tan3A=\\frac{3\\tan A-\\tan^3A}{1-3\\tan^2A}"},{"q":"Half-angle (power reduction)","f":"\\sin^2\\tfrac A2=\\frac{1-\\cos A}2,\\quad\\cos^2\\tfrac A2=\\frac{1+\\cos A}2,\\quad\\tan\\tfrac A2=\\frac{1-\\cos A}{\\sin A}=\\frac{\\sin A}{1+\\cos A}"},{"q":"Product of sines at 60° spacing","f":"\\sin\\theta\\sin(60^\\circ-\\theta)\\sin(60^\\circ+\\theta)=\\tfrac14\\sin3\\theta","n":"Same pattern: $\\cos\\theta\\cos(60^\\circ-\\theta)\\cos(60^\\circ+\\theta)=\\frac14\\cos3\\theta$, $\\tan\\theta\\tan(60^\\circ-\\theta)\\tan(60^\\circ+\\theta)=\\tan3\\theta$."},{"q":"$\\sin 2A$, $\\cos 2A$ in terms of $\\tan A$","f":"\\sin2A=\\frac{2t}{1+t^2},\\quad\\cos2A=\\frac{1-t^2}{1+t^2},\\quad\\tan2A=\\frac{2t}{1-t^2},\\ t=\\tan A"},{"q":"$1\\pm\\cos$ and $1\\pm\\sin$","f":"1+\\cos2A=2\\cos^2A,\\quad1-\\cos2A=2\\sin^2A,\\quad1\\pm\\sin2A=(\\sin A\\pm\\cos A)^2"},{"q":"Cubes from triple angle","f":"\\sin^3A=\\frac{3\\sin A-\\sin3A}4,\\qquad\\cos^3A=\\frac{3\\cos A+\\cos3A}4"},{"q":"Power reduction for fourth powers","f":"\\sin^4A+\\cos^4A=1-\\tfrac12\\sin^22A,\\qquad\\sin^6A+\\cos^6A=1-\\tfrac34\\sin^22A"},{"q":"Half-angle sign choice","f":"\\sin\\frac A2=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos A}2},\\ \\text{sign from the quadrant of } \\frac A2","n":"$\\sin\\frac A2+\\cos\\frac A2=\\pm\\sqrt{1+\\sin A}$."},{"q":"$\\tan\\frac A2$ in terms of $\\tan A$","f":"\\tan\\frac A2=\\frac{-1\\pm\\sqrt{1+\\tan^2A}}{\\tan A}"},{"q":"$\\sin 4A$, $\\cos 4A$","f":"\\cos4A=8\\cos^4A-8\\cos^2A+1,\\qquad\\sin4A=4\\sin A\\cos A(1-2\\sin^2A)"}]],["Sum–product",[{"q":"Sum to product","f":"\\sin C+\\sin D=2\\sin\\tfrac{C+D}2\\cos\\tfrac{C-D}2,\\qquad\\sin C-\\sin D=2\\cos\\tfrac{C+D}2\\sin\\tfrac{C-D}2","n":"$\\cos C+\\cos D=2\\cos\\frac{C+D}2\\cos\\frac{C-D}2$, $\\cos C-\\cos D=-2\\sin\\frac{C+D}2\\sin\\frac{C-D}2$."},{"q":"Product to sum","f":"2\\sin A\\cos B=\\sin(A+B)+\\sin(A-B),\\quad2\\cos A\\cos B=\\cos(A+B)+\\cos(A-B)","n":"$2\\sin A\\sin B=\\cos(A-B)-\\cos(A+B)$."},{"q":"Sum of two sines equal to product forms","f":"\\sin A+\\cos A=\\sqrt2\\sin\\left(A+\\tfrac\\pi4\\right),\\qquad\\sin A-\\cos A=\\sqrt2\\sin\\left(A-\\tfrac\\pi4\\right)"},{"q":"$\\sqrt3\\sin x+\\cos x$ type","f":"\\sqrt3\\sin x+\\cos x=2\\sin\\left(x+\\tfrac\\pi6\\right),\\qquad\\sin x+\\sqrt3\\cos x=2\\sin\\left(x+\\tfrac\\pi3\\right)"}]],["Series and products",[{"q":"Sum of sines in AP","f":"\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\\sin(\\alpha+k\\beta)=\\frac{\\sin\\frac{n\\beta}2}{\\sin\\frac\\beta2}\\sin\\left(\\alpha+\\frac{(n-1)\\beta}2\\right)","n":"For cosines replace the last $\\sin$ with $\\cos$. Hook: (sin of n×half-difference / sin of half-difference) × sin of average angle.","d":"Multiply by $2\\sin\\frac\\beta2$; each term becomes a difference of cosines that telescopes."},{"q":"Product of cosines in GP of angles","f":"\\cos A\\cos2A\\cos4A\\cdots\\cos2^{n-1}A=\\frac{\\sin2^nA}{2^n\\sin A}","d":"Multiply and divide by $2\\sin A$ and use $2\\sin x\\cos x=\\sin2x$ repeatedly."},{"q":"Sum of cosines in AP","f":"\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\\cos(\\alpha+k\\beta)=\\frac{\\sin\\frac{n\\beta}2}{\\sin\\frac\\beta2}\\cos\\left(\\alpha+\\frac{(n-1)\\beta}2\\right)"},{"q":"Sum $\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{n}$-type","f":"\\sum_{k=1}^{n-1}\\cos\\frac{2k\\pi}n=-1,\\qquad\\sum_{k=1}^{n-1}\\sin\\frac{k\\pi}n=\\cot\\frac\\pi{2n}"},{"q":"Product of sines $\\prod\\sin\\frac{k\\pi}n$","f":"\\prod_{k=1}^{n-1}\\sin\\frac{k\\pi}n=\\frac n{2^{n-1}}"},{"q":"Telescoping with $\\tan$","f":"\\tan A=\\cot A-2\\cot2A\\ \\Rightarrow\\ \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\\frac1{2^k}\\tan\\frac x{2^k}=\\frac1{2^{n-1}}\\cot\\frac x{2^{n-1}}-2\\cot2x"},{"q":"Telescoping with $\\csc 2A$","f":"\\csc2A=\\cot A-\\cot2A"}]],["Range and maxima",[{"q":"Range of $a\\sin\\theta+b\\cos\\theta$","f":"-\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}\\le a\\sin\\theta+b\\cos\\theta\\le\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}","d":"Write $a\\sin\\theta+b\\cos\\theta=\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}\\sin(\\theta+\\phi)$ with $\\tan\\phi=\\frac ba$."},{"q":"Minimum of $a\\tan^2\\theta+b\\cot^2\\theta$","f":"2\\sqrt{ab}\\quad(a,b>0)","n":"Similarly $a\\sin^2\\theta+b\\csc^2\\theta$ has minimum $2\\sqrt{ab}$ only if $a\\ge b$, else $a+b$."},{"q":"Range of $a\\sin^2x+b\\sin x\\cos x+c\\cos^2x$","f":"\\frac{a+c}2\\pm\\frac12\\sqrt{(a-c)^2+b^2}"},{"q":"Range of $a\\cos x+b\\sin x+c$","f":"\\left[c-\\sqrt{a^2+b^2},\\ c+\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}\\right]"},{"q":"Range of $\\sin^nx+\\cos^nx$","f":"\\sin^2x+\\cos^2x=1;\\quad\\sin^4x+\\cos^4x\\in\\left[\\tfrac12,1\\right];\\quad\\sin^6x+\\cos^6x\\in\\left[\\tfrac14,1\\right]"},{"q":"Maximum of $\\sin A\\sin B\\sin C$ and $\\cos A\\cos B\\cos C$ in a triangle","f":"\\sin A\\sin B\\sin C\\le\\frac{3\\sqrt3}8,\\qquad\\cos A\\cos B\\cos C\\le\\frac18"},{"q":"Bounds on sums in a triangle","f":"\\sin A+\\sin B+\\sin C\\le\\frac{3\\sqrt3}2,\\quad\\cos A+\\cos B+\\cos C\\le\\frac32,\\quad\\tan A+\\tan B+\\tan C\\ge3\\sqrt3\\ (\\text{acute})"}]],["Common results",[{"q":"Conditional identities when $A+B+C=\\pi$","f":"\\tan A+\\tan B+\\tan C=\\tan A\\tan B\\tan C","n":"Also $\\cot\\frac A2\\cot\\frac B2\\cot\\frac C2=\\sum\\cot\\frac A2$ and $\\sum\\tan\\frac A2\\tan\\frac B2=1$."},{"q":"Sine/cosine sums in a triangle","f":"\\sin2A+\\sin2B+\\sin2C=4\\sin A\\sin B\\sin C,\\qquad \\cos2A+\\cos2B+\\cos2C=-1-4\\cos A\\cos B\\cos C","n":"$\\sin A+\\sin B+\\sin C=4\\cos\\frac A2\\cos\\frac B2\\cos\\frac C2$; $\\cos A+\\cos B+\\cos C=1+4\\sin\\frac A2\\sin\\frac B2\\sin\\frac C2$."},{"q":"Squares in a triangle","f":"\\cos^2A+\\cos^2B+\\cos^2C=1-2\\cos A\\cos B\\cos C"},{"q":"Useful products","f":"\\cos20^\\circ\\cos40^\\circ\\cos80^\\circ=\\tfrac18,\\quad\\sin20^\\circ\\sin40^\\circ\\sin80^\\circ=\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}8,\\quad\\tan20^\\circ\\tan40^\\circ\\tan80^\\circ=\\sqrt3"},{"q":"Useful sums","f":"\\cos\\tfrac{2\\pi}7+\\cos\\tfrac{4\\pi}7+\\cos\\tfrac{6\\pi}7=-\\tfrac12,\\qquad\\cos\\tfrac{\\pi}{7}\\cos\\tfrac{2\\pi}7\\cos\\tfrac{4\\pi}7=-\\tfrac18"},{"q":"Bounds","f":"\\sin\\theta<\\theta<\\tan\\theta\\quad(0<\\theta<\\tfrac\\pi2)"},{"q":"Conditional identities (more), $A+B+C=\\pi$","f":"\\sin^2A+\\sin^2B+\\sin^2C=2+2\\cos A\\cos B\\cos C"},{"q":"$\\tan\\frac A2$ sums, $A+B+C=\\pi$","f":"\\tan\\frac A2\\tan\\frac B2+\\tan\\frac B2\\tan\\frac C2+\\tan\\frac C2\\tan\\frac A2=1"},{"q":"When $A+B+C=\\frac\\pi2$","f":"\\tan A\\tan B+\\tan B\\tan C+\\tan C\\tan A=1,\\qquad\\cot A+\\cot B+\\cot C=\\cot A\\cot B\\cot C"},{"q":"Product $\\cos A\\cos2A\\cdots$ special values","f":"\\cos\\frac\\pi9\\cos\\frac{2\\pi}9\\cos\\frac{4\\pi}9=\\frac18,\\qquad\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{15}\\cos\\frac{2\\pi}{15}\\cos\\frac{4\\pi}{15}\\cos\\frac{8\\pi}{15}=-\\frac1{16}"},{"q":"Sum $\\sin^2$ over equally spaced angles","f":"\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\\sin^2\\left(\\theta+\\frac{k\\pi}n\\right)=\\frac n2\\quad(n\\ge2)"},{"q":"Elimination tricks","f":"x=a\\cos\\theta+b\\sin\\theta,\\ y=a\\sin\\theta-b\\cos\\theta\\Rightarrow x^2+y^2=a^2+b^2"}]],["If this type comes, solve like this",[{"q":"If a product like $\\sin10^\\circ\\sin30^\\circ\\sin50^\\circ\\sin70^\\circ$ or $\\prod\\sin\\frac{k\\pi}{22}$","f":"\\sin\\theta\\sin(60^\\circ-\\theta)\\sin(60^\\circ+\\theta)=\\tfrac14\\sin3\\theta;\\ \\ \\prod\\cos2^k\\theta=\\frac{\\sin2^n\\theta}{2^n\\sin\\theta}","n":"Use complementary angles to turn sines into cosines of doubling angles, then the GP-product formula.","p":"4 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 13 times"},{"q":"If $\\cos^2A-\\sin^2B$ or $\\cos^2A-\\cos A\\cos B+\\cos^2B$ with special angles","f":"\\cos^2A-\\sin^2B=\\cos(A+B)\\cos(A-B)","p":"4 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 13 times"},{"q":"If $\\cos(\\alpha+\\beta)$, $\\sin(\\alpha-\\beta)$ given and $\\tan2\\alpha$ etc. asked","f":"2\\alpha=(\\alpha+\\beta)+(\\alpha-\\beta)","p":"1 PYQ (2019–2026) · asked 8 times"},{"q":"If the max/min of an expression in $\\sin$, $\\cos$","f":"a\\sin x+b\\cos x\\in[-\\sqrt{a^2+b^2},\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}];\\ \\ \\text{quadratic in } \\sin x:\\ \\text{restrict } t\\in[-1,1]","p":"4 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 12 times"},{"q":"If it is a heights-and-distances problem","f":"\\tan(\\text{elevation})=\\frac{\\text{height}}{\\text{horizontal distance}}","n":"Draw the figure, label distances with one variable, write two $\\tan$ equations, eliminate. Reflection in a lake: image is as far below the surface as the object is above.","p":"7 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 23 times"},{"q":"If a sum of $\\sec$ products telescopes","f":"\\sec A\\sec B=\\frac{\\tan B-\\tan A}{\\sin(B-A)}","p":"1 PYQ (2019–2026) · asked 3 times"},{"q":"If $\\tan$ of four related angles, $\\tan(x+100)=\\tan(x+50)\\tan x\\tan(x-50)$","f":"\\text{write as } \\frac{\\tan(x+100)}{\\tan(x-50)}=\\tan(x+50)\\tan x,\\ \\text{use componendo–dividendo}","p":"1 PYQ (2019–2026) · asked 5 times"},{"q":"If roots of a quadratic with $\\sin^4+\\cos^4$ coefficients must be real","f":"\\sin^4+\\cos^4=1-\\tfrac12\\sin^22\\theta,\\ \\ \\sin^6+\\cos^6=1-\\tfrac34\\sin^22\\theta","p":"1 PYQ (2019–2026) · asked 7 times"},{"q":"If a sum like $\\cos\\frac{2\\pi}7+\\cos\\frac{4\\pi}7+\\cos\\frac{6\\pi}7$","f":"=-\\tfrac12","p":"3 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 3 times"}]]]}